# Cursor Editor — Claude Code CLI Tool

## Overview

Claude Code is Cursor's standalone CLI tool that runs AI agent sessions from the terminal. It provides the same agent capabilities as the Cursor editor — code generation, refactoring, debugging, file operations — but in a headless, terminal-first environment. This makes it suitable for DevOps pipelines, CI/CD automation, remote servers, and developers who prefer terminal workflows.

### How It Differs from the Editor Agent

| Aspect | Editor Agent | Claude Code CLI |
|--------|-------------|-----------------|
| **Interface** | GUI (Composer panel, side bar) | Terminal (stdin/stdout) |
| **File interaction** | Editor with live diff views | File system operations via tools |
| **Context** | Open files, selected code, tabs | Working directory, explicitly passed files |
| **Input** | Click and type in UI | Terminal input, pipe, or script |
| **Output** | Rendered in Composer | Text output to terminal |
| **Best for** | Interactive development | Automation, CI/CD, remote servers |
| **Persistence** | Sessions saved in editor | Sessions managed via `--resume` |

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Developer] --> B{Where are you?}
    B -->|In Cursor Editor| C[Use Composer Cmd+K/L]
    B -->|In Terminal| D[Use Claude Code CLI]
    B -->|In CI/CD Pipeline| E[Use Claude Code CLI --headless]
    
    C --> F[GUI interactions]
    F --> G[Live editor feedback]
    
    D --> H[Terminal interactions]
    H --> I[Stdout/stderr output]
    
    E --> J[Non-interactive mode]
    J --> K[Exit codes for automation]
    
    G --> L[Same AI capabilities]
    I --> L
    K --> L
```

