## Model and Provider Configuration

### CLI Provider Selection

```bash
# Use a specific model
claude --model claude-sonnet-4-20250514 "Fix the bug"

# Use a specific provider
claude --provider anthropic "Analyze the code"

# Use a custom endpoint
claude --base-url http://localhost:11434/v1 --model codellama:7b "Explain this code"

# Use auto-selected model
claude --model auto "Refactor the module"
```

### Settings Precedence

Model/provider settings are resolved in this order (highest to lowest priority):

1. Command-line flags (`--model`, `--provider`, `--base-url`)
2. Environment variables (`CURSOR_API_KEY`, `CURSOR_MODEL`)
3. Cursor Settings (same as editor)
4. Default built-in model (`composer-2.5`)

### Environment Variables

| Variable | Purpose | Example |
|----------|---------|---------|
| `CURSOR_API_KEY` | Authentication for Cursor API | `CURSOR_API_KEY=cursor_abc123` |
| `CURSOR_MODEL` | Default model for all runs | `CURSOR_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-20250514` |
| `CURSOR_PROVIDER` | Default provider | `CURSOR_PROVIDER=anthropic` |
| `CURSOR_BASE_URL` | Custom API endpoint | `CURSOR_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1` |
| `CURSOR_MAX_TURNS` | Default max conversation turns | `CURSOR_MAX_TURNS=50` |

