## Session Management

### Agent Lifecycle

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Idle
    Idle --> Running: claude [prompt]
    Running --> Streaming: Agent sends messages
    Streaming --> Completing: All turns done
    Completing --> Idle: Exit code 0
    Running --> Error: Agent exception
    Error --> Idle: Exit code 1 or 2
    
    state Running {
        [*] --> Initializing
        Initializing --> Executing: Context loaded
        Executing --> ToolUse: Agent calls tool
        ToolUse --> Executing: Tool returns
        Executing --> Completing: No more work
        Executing --> Error: Max turns exceeded
    }
```

### Resume Mechanism

```bash
# Start a long-running task
claude --model claude-sonnet-4-20250514 "Analyze the codebase and create a refactoring plan"

# Agent returns an ID (e.g., bc-abc123)
# Continue later with:
claude --resume bc-abc123 "Also add documentation for each refactored module"
```

### Session Timeouts

```bash
# Set a 2-hour session timeout
claude --session-timeout 2 "Long-running analysis"

# Default timeout is 1 hour
# After timeout, session is terminated and must be resumed
```

